    "roles": ["band_member", "composer"],
    "summary": "Ghanaian drummer, self-taught from fourteen and known as \"The Rhythm Man\", who played highlife in Accra with the Rhythm Aces, the Star Gazers and the Comets, moved to London in 1961 and co-founded Osibisa there in 1969 with Teddy Osei and Mac Tontoh. The band of Ghanaian and Caribbean players took Afro-rock into the charts with \"Sunshine Day\" and \"Dance the Body Music\"; he wrote or co-wrote many of its songs, \"Woyaya\" among them, and drummed with it into the early 1990s.",
    "handedness": "right",
    "kit_orientation": "right_handed"
  },
